    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0903" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 Ship Travel/6b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Roosevelt </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-06T11:10:00-05:00">October 6,
                            1935—11:10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your proclamation,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d681-f1"/> carrying out Section 6 of the
                    Neutrality Act,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d681-f2"/> dated October 5 is being given
                    to the press as having been issued concurrently with your arms embargo
                        proclamation.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d681-f3"/> The arms embargo proclamation
                    and your statement<anchor n="18" xml:id="d681-f4"/> were published in this
                    morning’s newspapers but due to the midnight hour of release Section 6
                    proclamation not being then quite ready was not printed this morning but will be
                    in the press Monday morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
